---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import VideoGrid from '../components/VideoGrid.astro';
import Video from '../components/Video.astro';

// ── HOW TO ADD A VIDEO ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// This page shows video in TWO places, and they must not overlap:
//   1. This reel grid: a click-to-play showcase near the top.
//   2. One embed under each "What we shoot" tile, so every service claim
//      is backed by an example (see the Video components further down).
// A video listed here must NOT also be embedded below, or the same reel
// plays twice on one page.
// `vimeo` is the id from the URL, or 'id/hash' for a private link, or ''
// for a "Coming soon" tile. Only REAL clients. No invented names.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const videos = [
  // The Ballet Ball recap the "Who we work with" section below describes in
  // detail (backstage access, dancers from multiple angles, the feel of the
  // night). The copy made that claim for weeks with no video behind it.
  { title: 'Ballet Ball Nashville', category: 'Gala recap · 2 min', vimeo: '920104582' },
  { title: 'Nolensville Dance Company', category: 'Studio promo', vimeo: '1192295930' },
  // Vimeo titles this one just "Elite Dance". TODO(geoff): say what separates
  // it from the Elite Dance piece embedded under Studio Promos below.
  { title: 'Elite Dance', category: 'Studio promo', vimeo: '869957340' },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Dance Recital Videography',
  description: 'Recital films, studio promos and season content for dance companies.',
  url: 'https://sdubmedia.com/dance/',
  serviceType: 'Dance Recital Videography',
  provider: { '@type': 'LocalBusiness', '@id': 'https://sdubmedia.com/#business', name: 'SDub Media' },
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Nashville' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Nolensville' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Franklin' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Brentwood' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Murfreesboro' },
  ],
  hasOfferCatalog: {
    '@type': 'OfferCatalog',
    name: 'Dance Recital Videography',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'Offer', name: 'Full recital coverage', price: '2500', priceCurrency: 'USD', availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock' },
      { '@type': 'Offer', name: 'In-studio promo video', price: '500', priceCurrency: 'USD', availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock' },
    ],
  },
};
---
<Layout title="Dance Recital Videography Nashville | SDub Media" description="Recital films from $2,500, plus studio promos and season content for Nashville-area dance companies. Real work for Elite Dance, Nolensville Dance Company, and Ballet Ball Nashville."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
<section>
  <div class="container-narrow text-center">
    <span class="eyebrow">For dance companies</span>
    <h1 style="text-wrap: balance;">The recital is the deadline. The rest of the year is the opportunity.</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">Every studio needs the recital filmed properly. We do that, and the part that fills next year's classes: a few shoot days across the season, cut into content you can post all year.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Talk about your season</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">See it in action</span>
      <h2>Work for dance studios and companies around Nashville.</h2>
    </div>
    {/* Three reels now fills the row, so `center` is no longer needed. Add it
        back if this ever drops below three. */}
    <VideoGrid items={videos} />

    {/* Recital stills. Four genres on purpose: a studio director needs to know
        we can shoot every number on their program, not just the ballet.
        Deliberately posed group shots, NOT frames of dancers mid-movement. The
        six videos above this already carry the motion; these do the job video
        cannot, which is showing the full range of the program in one glance,
        with no play button to press. Do not "upgrade" these to action frames:
        that would duplicate what the reels already prove. Recital content is
        cleared for publication (Geoff, 2026-07-30). */}
    <div class="wedding-strip" style="margin-top: 3rem;">
      <img src="/images/dance/hiphop-group.jpg" alt="A hip hop group posed on stage in magenta jackets under purple light" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
      <img src="/images/dance/acro-group.jpg" alt="An acro group holding balance and split positions on stage" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
      <img src="/images/dance/jazz-group.jpg" alt="A jazz group in green fringe costumes posed under green light" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
      <img src="/images/dance/ballet-group.jpg" alt="A character ballet number in pirate costume around a treasure chest" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
    </div>
    <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--muted);">Hip hop, acro, jazz, character ballet. We shoot every number on the program.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What we shoot</span>
      <h2>Three things a studio needs.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Recital and Performance Films</h3>
        <p>Multi-camera coverage, cut so parents can find their dancer. Full runtime for families, plus a short version worth putting on your website.</p>
        <div style="padding: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;">
          {/* The full 59-minute show as families receive it. Labeled with its
              runtime so nobody expects a highlight reel. TODO(geoff): name the
              studio, and swap in a 60-90s cut when one exists. */}
          <Video id="979509588" title="Full dance recital film, 59 minutes" />
          <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.6rem;">Full show, 59 minutes. This is the film families receive.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Studio Promos and Audition Reels</h3>
        <p>The video that runs while a parent decides between you and the studio across town. Your space, your teachers, your dancers. Not stock footage of somebody else's.</p>
        <div style="padding: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;">
          <Video id="839344212" title="Elite Dance studio highlights" />
          <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.6rem;">Elite Dance</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Season-Long Social Content</h3>
        <p>Class clips, competition trips, rehearsals, senior spotlights. A few shoot days a year become months of posts, which is the part studios never get around to.</p>
        <div style="padding: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;">
          <Video id="1214148467" title="Nolensville Dance Company season content" />
          <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.6rem;">Nolensville Dance Company</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Who we work with</span>
      <h2>Elite Dance, Nolensville Dance Company, Ballet Ball Nashville.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>Nolensville Dance Company</strong>: ongoing content</li>
      <li><strong>Elite Dance</strong>: studio highlight reels</li>
      <li><strong>Ballet Ball Nashville</strong>: full backstage access, dancers from multiple angles, the feel of the whole night</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">A locked-off camera at the back of the auditorium documents that a recital happened. It does not show anyone why your studio is worth driving across town for.</p>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">Most studios come to us for the recital, because that is the date on the calendar. The ones who stay find the ongoing content is what moves enrollment.</p>
    <div class="text-center" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Talk about your season</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Who shoots it</span>
      <h2>Specialists, not one person with a camera.</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">A recital is a live event with no second take, which is exactly the kind of day you do not want a generalist on.</p>
    {/* Roles only, never names or faces: the team is not willing to appear on
        the marketing site and that stays their call. These four roles are the
        confirmed set (see /about). Do not add a fifth to fill a page. */}
    <ul class="facts" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <li><strong>Two videographers cover the recital</strong>, so no number is seen from just one angle</li>
      <li><strong>Three photographers are on the team</strong>, including one who shoots nothing but live events, where every moment gets exactly one attempt</li>
      <li><strong>The owner is behind a camera</strong>, at the recital, not back at a desk</li>
      <li><strong>Editing stays in house</strong>, so the film is not sitting in someone else's queue while parents ask when it is coming</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">More on <a href="/about/">who shows up</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What it costs</span>
      <h2>The recital and the season price differently.</h2>
    </div>
    {/* Prices confirmed by Geoff 2026-08-13: $2,500 flat full recital coverage
        (full edited recital that OPENS with a highlight reel; per-number cuts
        for families are offered, price not published, so say "available" and
        never imply included or invent a number), $500 in-studio promo video.
        Published deliberately, same policy as the weddings page. Keep these
        accurate or remove them, never soften them back into estimates. */}
    <p style="font-size: 1.15rem;">The recital prices flat, and it is on the page so you can plan your season around it.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);">
        <span><strong>Full recital coverage</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">The whole program, start to finish. Your full edited recital opens with a highlight reel, and per-number cuts for families are available</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><strong>$2,500</strong></span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;">
        <span><strong>In-studio promo video</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">A short promo filmed at your studio, for filling classes the rest of the year</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><strong>$500</strong></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Ongoing content across a season is its own arrangement. Tell us what the year looks like and you will get a real number, not a range.</p>
    <div class="text-center" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Get a quote for your recital</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
